<title>UK: BTG signs pain killing drug agreement.</title>
<headline>BTG signs pain killing drug agreement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical to automotive group BTG Plc on Wednesday said it had signed an exclusive worldwide licence agreement with Forest Laboritories Inc to develop and market a new painkiller.</p>
<p>The new product combines an opiate analgesic, oxycodone, with an anti-inflammatory agent, ibuprofen. In preliminary human clinical trials these drugs may be beneficial when used in combination in treating moderate to severe post operative and muscular skeletal injury pain, the company said.</p>
<p>Terms of the agreement with Forest were not disclosed.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
